he length, in tenths, of the dashes in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed."}]}],"name":"dashLength"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The length, in tenths, of the spaces in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed."}]}],"name":"spaceLength"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}]}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}]}],"name":"placement"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The orientation attribute indicates whether slurs and ties are overhand (tips down) or underhand (tips up). This is distinct from the placement attribute used by any notation type."}]}],"name":"orientation"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type."}]}],"name":"bezierX"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type."}]}],"name":"bezierY"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type."}]}],"name":"bezierX2"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type."}]}],"name":"bezierY2"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point offset for one with a stop or continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"bezierOffset"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur with a continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX2"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"bezierOffset2"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}],"name":"color"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"init","title":"init(id:kind:number:lineKind:dashLength:spaceLength:position:placement:orientation:bezierX:bezierY:bezierX2:bezierY2:bezierOffset:bezierOffset2:color:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStopContinue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLStartStopContinueO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lineKind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLineKind","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11M